<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Parakramabahu III</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. 1287–1293</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Parakramabahu III was a king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sri-lanka">Sri Lanka</a> who reigned from 1287 to 1293, ruling from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polonnaruwa">Polonnaruwa</a>. After a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pandya-dynasty">Pandya</a> army under Aryacakravarti had taken the fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yapahuwa">Yapahuwa</a> and carried off the Tooth Relic of the Buddha, he went to the Pandya court and recovered the relic by negotiation, according to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/culavamsa">Culavamsa</a>.</p></div>
